From 63dd48a7056bb44727b5a2f3f01002345c899560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: divyam234 <47589864+divyam234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 13:53:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add --rpc-listen-socket option for Unix domain socket RPC

Adds support for listening on a Unix domain socket for JSON-RPC/XML-RPC
connections, as an alternative to TCP port listening.

New option:
  --rpc-listen-socket=PATH  Specify a Unix domain socket path for
                            JSON-RPC/XML-RPC server to listen to.

- New SocketCore::bindUnixSocket() creates and binds AF_UNIX socket,
  automatically removing any existing socket file at the path
- New UnixListenCommand class, analogous to HttpListenCommand,
  accepts connections and passes them to HttpServerCommand
- When --rpc-listen-socket is specified, TCP port listening is skipped
  (--rpc-listen-port and --rpc-listen-socket are mutually exclusive)
- Socket file is cleaned up on shutdown
- Guarded with HAVE_SYS_UN_H for platforms without Unix socket support
